There's some new constants that can be used for these now, though they're hidden in generated files:
in <xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Create/common.hpp>, you can use Create::interface, Create::instance_path, and even Create::default_service:

```
namespace sdbusplus::common::xyz::openbmc_project::logging
{

struct Create
{
    static constexpr auto interface = "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Create";

    enum class FFDCFormat
    {
        JSON,
        CBOR,
        Text,
        Custom,
    };

    static constexpr auto instance_path = "/xyz/openbmc_project/logging";
    static constexpr auto default_service = "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging";
   ...
  };
 ```

though I think it's fine to use still the mapper instead of default_service.

If there's a common place that creates the additional data, can you also add:

 additionalData.emplace("_PID", std::to_string(getpid()));

That _PID then lets the phosphor-logging daemon find the application name
